Third-party content in the `hw/` subtree
----------------------------------------

`hw/vendor/odin/` is a byte-identical copy of the ODIN spiking neuromorphic
processor RTL from https://github.com/ChFrenkel/ODIN at commit 1781931,
Copyright (C) 2016-2019 Université catholique de Louvain (UCLouvain), Belgium.
Its Verilog sources are licensed under the Solderpad Hardware License,
Version 2.0 ("SHL-2.0", https://solderpad.org/licenses/SHL-2.0/) — see
`hw/vendor/odin/LICENSE` — and its documentation under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License — see `hw/vendor/odin/doc/LICENSE`.
Every upstream per-file copyright header is retained verbatim.

`hw/fpga/mem/` and `hw/gen/` contain Modified Works derived from that RTL.
`hw/fpga/mem/` is the upstream-mandated substitution of the behavioral SRAM
models by synthesizable, BRAM-inferable memories with identical module names,
ports and timing. `hw/gen/` holds the variant-core TEMPLATES the mimarsinan
generator expands (`src/mimarsinan/mapping/export/odin_gen/`): a LIF-only,
open-loop core whose geometry, membrane register and soma law are parameters,
with a direct synchronous configuration port in place of the SPI slave. Per
SHL-2.0 section 4(b), each such file — the template and every file generated
from it — carries the UCLouvain copyright notice, the Solderpad licence notice,
and a prominent statement of the changes made relative to the upstream work it
derives from.

`hw/tb/` contains original mimarsinan testbench sources (MIT, as above); they
instantiate the vendored core but derive no text from it.

